342:IM-1 measures the residual of fitting GMAT EarthFixed Z as `u(t)·r_TOE`, rather than a propagated trajectory error. The quadratic-only nine-parameter fit and full fifteen-parameter fit use two spacecraft, 896 epochs from 0 through 53700 s, and km-to-m conversion. My QR result differs from the stored quadratic RMS by 2.25e-11 m, comfortably within 1e-6 m. The documented conditioning-based rounding scale supports a practical reproduction tolerance; no cross-BLAS worst-case error theorem was independently established.
